s financial structure and gives it the visibility needed to continue executing its operational and debt reduction plan, the trajectory of which is based on two pillars: ",{"type":"b","children":["disposals of non-strategic assets"]}," with a cumulative target of around €100m and a ",{"type":"b","children":["planned inventory reduction "]},"of €100m over 4 years."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Outlook"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["The Group intends to maintain its ",{"type":"b","children":["commercial momentum"]}," in the second half of 2026 by focusing on the development of its ",{"type":"b","children":["premium cuvées"]}," and strengthening its positions in its main markets."]},{"type":"p","children":["The gradual roll-out of ",{"type":"b","children":["Champagne Pompadour"]}," and the continuation of the premiumization strategy around the Cuvée Louise and Apanage 1874 range from ",{"type":"b","children":["Maison Pommery \u0026 Greno"]}," should enable the Group to continue strengthening its operating margin in the second half of the year."]},{"type":"p","children":["The ",{"type":"b","children":["earliest harvest"]}," in the history of Champagne has just come to an end in an exceptional climatic context, with remarkably high-quality grapes despite low agronomic yields."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Dividend"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["At its Annual General Meeting on October 19, 2026, Maison Pommery \u0026 Associés will propose the payment of a dividend for the 2025 financial year of ",{"type":"b","children":["€0.38 per share"]},". This dividend will be paid on Monday, December 14, 2026 and would correspond to a gross yield of 3.89% based on the share price on September 4, 2026."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Next communication"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Publication of 2026 turnover: ",{"type":"b","children":["January 28, 2027"]},", after market close"]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","childr